<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mount Batukaru</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mount Batukaru is a volcano in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, and the second-highest peak on the island, at about 2,276 metres. Its slopes feed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> terraces of Tabanan, including those of Jatiluwih, part of the subak irrigation landscape listed as a World Heritage Site. Pura Luhur Batukaru on its flank is one of Bali's principal temples.</p></div>
